# Task FEATURE-006-US-002-T01 — Implement: Access control enforcement

> **DaemonCore coding-agent prompt.** Work type: `feature` · Size: `M` · Priority: `P2` · Status: `todo`

## Where this fits
- **Epic EPIC-006 — Sharing Platform.** Allow users to share models with controlled visibility (public, private, unlisted), shareable URLs and clean read-only public views.
- **Feature FEATURE-006 — Sharing Platform — implementation.**
- **Story FEATURE-006-US-002 — Access control enforcement.** _As an owner, I want access enforced server-side so visibility can't be bypassed._

## Objective
As an owner, I want access enforced server-side so visibility can't be bypassed.

## What to do
Implement the capability so that every acceptance criterion below holds. Specifically:
- Access checks gate every model read/write
- Enforcement covered by tests
Add or update docstrings and any necessary types. Keep the change focused on this story; do not pull in scope from other stories/epics.

## Acceptance criteria (Definition of Done)
- [ ] Access checks gate every model read/write
- [ ] Enforcement covered by tests
- [ ] New/updated tests pass and cover the above
- [ ] No regression in the existing `pytest` suite

## Dependencies
None within this story. (Respect cross-epic dependencies of the parent epic.)

## Project conventions
- Target Python 3.13. Use British spelling in all user-facing text.
- Keep the pure model layer (`model/`) free of Streamlit; `app.py` is UI/render only.
- Pin any new runtime deps in `requirements.txt`; test-only deps in `requirements-dev.txt`.
- Write deterministic `pytest` tests; follow the style of `tests/test_fiscal_model.py`.
- Match the surrounding code style. Prefer small, coherent diffs over broad refactors.
- Update `README.md` / `docs/` whenever behaviour changes.

## Guardrails (EPIC-006)
- Default visibility is private; publishing is an explicit action.
- Enforce access server-side; private data must never leak to non-owners.
- Unlisted models use unguessable ids; public views are strictly read-only.

